  "body": "Work package: https://openproject.romaine.life/wp/TMUX-21\n\nThe standalone folder picker now builds for macOS (arm64), so the work Mac's `launch-claude` can call the real picker instead of its plain-`fzt` stand-in. Windows-only code (hidden/system attributes, bringing the console forward) moves to `_windows.go` files; macOS hides dot names and `UF_HIDDEN`, as Finder does. A new `build-macos` CI job vets, tests and builds natively and adds `fzt-picker-frontend-darwin-arm64` to each release; the Windows binaries and `publish.ps1` are unchanged.\n\nAlso fixes drive roots' `Original` gaining a stray `\\` on `/`, and replaces the MACOS.md handoff with the final docs in CLAUDE.md. Not done here: installing it on the Mac and switching `launch-claude` (shell-config-profile-4).\n",
